WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.832
In the Northern Song, there was an official named Bao Zheng, whose name everyone remembers.

00:00:06.182 --> 00:00:10.694
He served honestly and uprightly, and the people trusted him deeply.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:18.700
Bao Zheng had a dark face; as an official he was honest and upright, and never accepted bribes.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:25.266
When ordinary people suffered injustice, they liked to bring their cases to Bao Zheng, because he would surely uphold justice.

00:00:25.616 --> 00:00:29.912
He listened carefully to every word and investigated until the truth was clear.

00:00:30.262 --> 00:00:35.350
No matter how powerful the other party was, if they broke the law, Bao Zheng dared to punish them.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:42.300
Later, people turned his stories into operas and novels, and respectfully called him 'Bao the Blue Sky'.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:48.074
On stage, Lord Bao even has a crescent moon on his forehead.

00:00:48.424 --> 00:00:55.816
Although some stories are legends, Bao Zheng's image as an honest official has been passed down to this day.

00:00:56.166 --> 00:01:00.030
Whenever people speak of honest officials, they think of Bao Zheng.

